1
00:01:23,289 --> 00:01:25,220
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:27,457
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:01:28,322 --> 00:01:32,082
اَلْحَمْدُ لله رَبِّ الْعَلَمِيْنَ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد

4
00:01:32,618 --> 00:01:35,202
وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراً

5
00:01:35,652 --> 00:01:36,936
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ الله

6
00:01:38,377 --> 00:01:41,339
This is beginning of our second week In Sha Allah Ta'ala(إن شاءالله تعالى)

7
00:01:42,173 --> 00:01:44,794
on the series of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

8
00:01:47,238 --> 00:01:48,810
On Friday we were talking about

9
00:01:51,334 --> 00:01:56,162
some of the freedoms that were granted by the Khalifah(خليفه).

10
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:02,872
We move on to the freedom of property or Hurriyyat-Tamalluk(حريةالتملك)

11
00:02:02,908 --> 00:02:05,131
but in English we would call it, Property Rights.

12
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:08,278
It's more of right then freedom(of property), it's rights.

13
00:02:09,918 --> 00:02:16,341
And the Khilafah(خلافة) granted the Muslims  property rights

14
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:26,593
and not only that but sometimes, it would give out, hand out to the citizens, property.

15
00:02:28,619 --> 00:02:35,220
Such was the case with Rasool Allah ﷺ who gave Bilal Ibn Rabah رضي الله عنه a large piece of land,

16
00:02:35,242 --> 00:02:36,855
very large piece of land.

17
00:02:39,317 --> 00:02:41,750
Now, since the population was expanding,

18
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:46,730
and the size of the Khilafah(خلافة) was expanding and number of Muslims was going up,

19
00:02:50,532 --> 00:02:54,632
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, he went to Bilal Ibn Rabah(بلال ابن رباح), and he told him,

20
00:02:55,035 --> 00:03:01,559
Rasool Allah ﷺ has given you a large piece of land and you are unable to cultivate it all,

21
00:03:01,745 --> 00:03:06,245
it was either pasture land or it was agricultural land,

22
00:03:06,362 --> 00:03:15,342
and Bilal(بلال) wasn't able to invest all of that land, so part of the land was still wasted.

23
00:03:16,185 --> 00:03:17,657
So Bilal Ibn Rabah(بلال ابن رباح) said: "Yes".

24
00:03:18,135 --> 00:03:24,735
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Then, I want you to hand me over, the land, which you are not cultivating.

25
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:30,580
Bilal(بلال) responded and said: "I am not gonna give you something that was given to me by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

26
00:03:30,681 --> 00:03:33,081
No way! I am going to give you this land back.!

27
00:03:34,384 --> 00:03:35,984
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "Yes you will"!

28
00:03:36,711 --> 00:03:43,111
And he took away from him the part that was not cultivated and he distributed it, among the Muslims.

29
00:03:44,027 --> 00:03:48,727
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) did not want people to hold up these pieces of land,

30
00:03:49,952 --> 00:03:55,052
when they could be given to other Muslims, who will cultivate them.

31
00:03:55,626 --> 00:03:58,526
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted the benefit of the whole.

32
00:03:59,414 --> 00:04:02,014
 While Bilal Ibn Rabah(بلال ابن رباح) was looking at it that,

33
00:04:02,078 --> 00:04:04,478
this was the piece of land that was given to me by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

34
00:04:06,123 --> 00:04:09,948
So, anyway, he took it away, and distributed it to the Muslims.

35
00:04:10,028 --> 00:04:15,432
So, the point to learn here is that "property needs to be invested."

36
00:04:15,564 --> 00:04:20,764
it needs to be cultivated and not just left like that.

37
00:04:21,194 --> 00:04:26,938
and this shows you the interest that the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) had in promoting trade and commerce.

38
00:04:30,696 --> 00:04:37,833
FREEDOM OF EXPRESSION AND SPEAKING.

39
00:04:41,357 --> 00:04:47,657
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is the Khalifah(خليفه) and he meets a man, who just came out of a court.

40
00:04:49,994 --> 00:04:52,394
 Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) use to judge

41
00:04:54,224 --> 00:04:56,568
in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he was a Qadhi(قاضي).

42
00:04:58,903 --> 00:05:01,603
 So this man came out and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told him;

43
00:05:03,077 --> 00:05:06,077
What was the ruling of Ali(علي) and Zayd(زيد)?

44
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:09,020
" So, the man said: "so and so."

45
00:05:09,271 --> 00:05:12,571
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "If it was me, I would have ruled otherwise".

46
00:05:14,928 --> 00:05:20,428
 So, the man said: "What prevents you from doing so, if you are the Ameer(امير) of the Believers?"

47
00:05:22,327 --> 00:05:27,227
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "If this was an issue that straight goes to the book of Allah

48
00:05:27,374 --> 00:05:32,074
 or the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ I would enforce my ruling

49
00:05:32,555 --> 00:05:37,051
but this is my opinion and my opinion is as good as opinion of Zayd(زيد) and Ali(علي)."

50
00:05:39,355 --> 00:05:45,855
So, he went along with the ruling of Zayd(زيد) and Ali Ibn Abi Talibرضي الله عنهما,

51
00:05:45,907 --> 00:05:50,107
even though it is contrary to what he thinks, is the right ruling,

52
00:05:50,398 --> 00:05:55,898
and that shows you the freedom of expression that existed in the time of Khalifah(خليفه)

53
00:05:55,960 --> 00:06:00,460
he didn’t enforce his opinion on Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه and Zayd(زيد).

54
00:06:06,179 --> 00:06:12,379
He was once giving Khutba(خطبه) and he told the Muslims,

55
00:06:15,255 --> 00:06:25,087
If you see any crookedness in me, then I want you to fix it, to make it straight.

56
00:06:26,797 --> 00:06:34,396
So a man stood up and he said: If we see any crookedness in you, we will straighten it with our swords".

57
00:06:36,709 --> 00:06:40,337
This was the very outspoken member of the society.

58
00:06:41,144 --> 00:06:45,728
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), did he call in, his security guards and say,

59
00:06:45,793 --> 00:06:50,193
this is terrorism against the state and this man must be thrown in jail,

60
00:06:50,288 --> 00:06:55,988
and we need to keep him away, he is harm to society?

61
00:06:56,550 --> 00:06:59,702
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "Alhamdulillah(الحمد لله)! Praise be to Allah!

62
00:07:01,153 --> 00:07:10,009
 Who has made in the Muslims someone, who will fix Umar(عمر), with his sword, if umar(عمر) goes wrong.

63
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:19,932
 Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله)! That Allah has granted me followers, that will straighten me up if I go wrong."

64
00:07:21,172 --> 00:07:27,044
 Umar(عُمَر) was happy, Umar(عُمَر) was happy that, this was the state of Ummah(امة) at that time.

65
00:07:28,049 --> 00:07:31,013
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wasn’t looking for submissive followers,

66
00:07:31,704 --> 00:07:35,476
 who would say this is Wali Al-Amr(ولى الامر), we'll just do, whatever he wants,

67
00:07:35,573 --> 00:07:40,773
he can take away our wealth, and lash, flog our backs and we will just say,

68
00:07:41,304 --> 00:07:42,425
سمعناواطعنا

69
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:43,250
We listen and obey!

70
00:07:43,366 --> 00:07:47,300
He could do right, we will follow him, he could do wrong we will follow him, we are just blind followers.

71
00:07:47,902 --> 00:07:51,402
 No, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted to make sure that, this wasn't the condition of the Ummah(امة).

72
00:07:51,784 --> 00:07:54,692
He wanted to make sure that the Ummah(امة) are only going to follow him, if he is right

73
00:07:55,255 --> 00:07:58,303
and they will stand up and correct him, if he is wrong.

74
00:08:00,003 --> 00:08:03,951
 And he was very happy when he saw that, somebody willing to use force to do that.

75
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:09,257
 Obviously this is something that Ummah(امة) needs to learn today.

76
00:08:09,736 --> 00:08:15,736
 Because the Ummah(امة) have became blind followers, submissive and they have given into to Zulm(ظلم).

77
00:08:16,343 --> 00:08:19,263
 They have accepted Zulm(ظلم) on themselves and others.

78
00:08:20,330 --> 00:08:24,898
And they have accepted this state of humiliation that the Ummah(امة) is going through.

79
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:28,140
The Ummah(امة) needs to stand up and fight for its rights.

80
00:08:29,027 --> 00:08:32,027
 If you don’t fight for it, you're not going to get it,

81
00:08:37,282 --> 00:08:40,116
 Amazing condition of the society.! Once he was giving the khutba(خطبة)

82
00:08:42,492 --> 00:08:44,692
 and he said: Is'mioo(اسمعو) Wa' Ati'oo(وأطيعو). Listen and Obey!

83
00:08:45,743 --> 00:08:48,843
One man stood and said: We are not going to listen and we are not going to obey.

84
00:08:50,025 --> 00:08:51,197
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "why?

85
00:08:52,647 --> 00:08:57,263
He said: Because, you have given us each, one piece of cloth and I see you wearing two pieces.

86
00:08:58,194 --> 00:09:02,222
This was some pieces of fabric that came into Madina,

87
00:09:02,411 --> 00:09:05,219
he gave it out and he gave everybody one piece.

88
00:09:05,632 --> 00:09:08,800
 And now, this man is seeing Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is wearing two pieces,

89
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:16,650
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "Call Abdullah(عبدالله)", his son Abdullah(عبدالله).

90
00:09:16,708 --> 00:09:19,008
 Umar(عُمَر) said: "I am not going to answer this, Abdullah(عبدالله) will".

91
00:09:19,638 --> 00:09:22,302
 So, he calls in his son Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) and he tells him;

92
00:09:22,834 --> 00:09:25,138
 "Tell them, how come I am wearing two pieces of cloth?"

93
00:09:26,442 --> 00:09:27,709
 Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said;

94
00:09:27,759 --> 00:09:30,711
لَئَنَّ أَبِيْ رَجُلٌ طَوِيْلَ الْقَامَةْ العَرِيْضَ الْمُنْكَبَيْنْ

95
00:09:30,762 --> 00:09:33,662
My father is a very tall man, with wide shoulders,

96
00:09:34,277 --> 00:09:38,165
so one piece of cloth is not enough for him, so I gave him mine.

97
00:09:40,579 --> 00:09:42,239
I gave him mine.

98
00:09:43,161 --> 00:09:46,869
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) did not take an additional piece from the Muslim Treasury.

99
00:09:48,876 --> 00:09:55,116
This shows you, how delicate the justice of Umar(عُمَر) was,

100
00:09:55,632 --> 00:09:59,792
and it shows you how delicate the standard of the Muslims was.

101
00:10:01,504 --> 00:10:10,144
They did not even accept for the Khalifah(خليفه) to have an additional piece of cloth, that they don't have.

102
00:10:11,609 --> 00:10:14,609
Very, very, very different standards than we have now.

103
00:10:15,445 --> 00:10:21,497
Some Muslims are even willing to be owned by the king or president.

104
00:10:23,932 --> 00:10:32,020
They see it as a rightful claim for the government to just take away your wealth,

105
00:10:32,124 --> 00:10:33,657
abuse the wealth of the Ummah(امة).

106
00:10:37,466 --> 00:10:44,266
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) another time was talking, giving a Khutba(خطبه)

107
00:10:45,915 --> 00:10:48,815
and he was angry that the Mahr(مهر) was going up.

108
00:10:49,496 --> 00:10:56,304
Mahr(مهر) is the dowry and Umar(عُمَر) wanted the dowry to be reasonable

109
00:10:56,734 --> 00:11:00,118
and he was quite upset that the prices were going up.

110
00:11:01,853 --> 00:11:06,301
So, he gives a Khutba(خطبه) and says the Mahr(مهر) should not go above this amount

111
00:11:06,752 --> 00:11:09,652
and if I hear that any Mahr(مهر) is over this amount,

112
00:11:09,971 --> 00:11:12,671
I am going to take the additional amount and put it in the treasury.

113
00:11:14,208 --> 00:11:17,064
 So, a woman stood up and old woman stood up and said:

114
00:11:17,503 --> 00:11:18,703
 "It's not up to you to do that."

115
00:11:19,633 --> 00:11:20,733
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "Why?"

116
00:11:20,976 --> 00:11:22,309
She said: because Allahعَزّوجَلّ says:

117
00:11:22,362 --> 00:11:24,196
وَآتَيْتُمْ اِحْدَاهُنَّ قِنْطَارَا

118
00:11:25,025 --> 00:11:29,493
It mentions in Qur’an that "You give the woman a Qintaar(قنطار)"

119
00:11:30,536 --> 00:11:34,520
 Allahعَزّوجَلّ was referring to some issues of marriage

120
00:11:34,575 --> 00:11:38,359
 and it mentions in the Ayah(آية) and Qintaar(قنطار) is a large amount of Gold.

121
00:11:41,594 --> 00:11:48,590
So, this woman used this as a Daleel(دليل) as an evidence that you can give Mahr(مهر) as much as a Qintaar(قنطار).

122
00:11:49,927 --> 00:11:54,927
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "A man was wrong and a woman was right."

123
00:11:57,083 --> 00:11:58,617
 In another narrations, it says:

124
00:11:58,665 --> 00:12:00,165
أَصَابَتْ اِمْرَأَةْ وَأَخْطَاءْ عُمر

125
00:12:00,293 --> 00:12:01,905
A woman was right and Umar(عُمَر) was wrong.

126
00:12:02,874 --> 00:12:04,574
 In a third narration, it says; that he said:

127
00:12:05,063 --> 00:12:07,263
كُلُّ اَحَدْ اَفْقَهْ مِنْ عمر

128
00:12:07,557 --> 00:12:09,091
"Everyone has more Fiqh(فقه) than me".

129
00:12:13,753 --> 00:12:18,041
 And these are the examples to show the, also not just the justice,

130
00:12:18,232 --> 00:12:22,004
 but it also shows the humbleness of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), you know

131
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:32,580
for somebody to stand up and just correct him in public, his pride didn’t take over, he accepted it.

132
00:12:33,450 --> 00:12:35,378
and he said, everybody has more Fiqh(فقه) than me.

133
00:12:40,827 --> 00:12:47,227
There are exception to this rule Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) just didn’t give a blanket freedom of expression

134
00:12:47,286 --> 00:12:49,622
to anyone and everyone to say whatever they want.

135
00:12:50,911 --> 00:12:56,571
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) placed restrictions just like we saw, he place restriction on property rights,

136
00:12:56,654 --> 00:12:59,874
he also placed restrictions on freedom of expression.

137
00:13:00,635 --> 00:13:04,871
 He was, once giving a Khutba(خطبه), and in the beginning of the Khutba(خطبه),

138
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:09,000
he make the opening of the Khutba(خطبه), and it says:

139
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:13,583
مَنْ يَهْدِالله فَلَا مُضِّلَّ لَهْ، وَمَنْ يُضْلِلِ لله فَلَا هَادِيَ لَهْ

140
00:13:13,861 --> 00:13:18,969
Whomever, Allah guides nobody can misguide him and whoever, Allah misguides nobody can guide him.

141
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:28,030
 So, this man stands up and Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم), if he was Muslim or not, any way he said;

142
00:13:29,589 --> 00:13:33,589
Allahعَزّوجَلّ does not misguide anyone, because it says;

143
00:13:33,963 --> 00:13:35,596
وَمَنْ يُضْلِلِ لله فَلَا هَادِيَ لَهْ

144
00:13:35,672 --> 00:13:38,036
And whoever Allah misguides, nobody can guide him.

145
00:13:38,536 --> 00:13:41,832
So, now he is bringing up a controversial issue in Qadar(قَدَر).

146
00:13:42,608 --> 00:13:47,008
And Qadar(قَدَر), Dear brothers and sisters is one area where we should belief,

147
00:13:47,624 --> 00:13:50,780
we should not try to delve into and try to comprehend,

148
00:13:51,113 --> 00:13:54,913
it's one area that should be taken as Eeman(ايمان) in Al-Ghaeb(الغيب).

149
00:13:55,225 --> 00:13:56,605
Belief in the unseen.

150
00:13:57,698 --> 00:13:58,251
Why?

151
00:13:58,473 --> 00:14:02,211
Because some aspects of Qadar(قَدَر) are beyond human comprehension.

152
00:14:03,187 --> 00:14:07,887
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has taught us the knowledge that we need to know, He didn’t teach us everything.

153
00:14:08,956 --> 00:14:12,876
Allah taught us in Qur’an things that we need to know.

154
00:14:13,169 --> 00:14:19,069
There are some things that, there are many aspects of knowledge that are not mentioned in the Qur'an

155
00:14:19,115 --> 00:14:23,639
because we don’t need them, we don't need them for Hidaya(هداية).

156
00:14:25,358 --> 00:14:27,958
So for example in Surat-Ul-Kahf(سورة الكهف).

157
00:14:29,985 --> 00:14:34,185
Some were debating, and this was mentioned in some of the books.

158
00:14:34,584 --> 00:14:37,984
They were debating on the Issue of the Dog.

159
00:14:38,122 --> 00:14:40,488
You know the dog of the people of the cave.

160
00:14:41,379 --> 00:14:44,079
People of the cave, they had a dog and this dog is mentioned in the Qur'an,

161
00:14:44,103 --> 00:14:47,103
وَكَلْبُهُمْ بَاسِطٌ ذِرَاعَيْهِ بِالْوَصِيدِ ۚ

162
00:14:48,491 --> 00:14:51,163
So, they were debating, what color is this dog?

163
00:14:52,461 --> 00:14:58,294
Is it black or white or is it black and white or is it red or yellow.?

164
00:14:59,901 --> 00:15:01,235
 What's the benefit of such knowledge?

165
00:15:01,871 --> 00:15:05,539
 What will you gain by knowing the color of the dog? NOTHING.!

166
00:15:06,057 --> 00:15:06,697
عِلْم لَا يَنْفَعْ

167
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:08,346
This is knowledge that does not benefit.

168
00:15:08,544 --> 00:15:10,377
 Therefore, it wasn’t mentioned to us.

169
00:15:11,637 --> 00:15:20,285
 You find that Qur’an does not mention the details of time, of names, of locations,

170
00:15:20,725 --> 00:15:25,777
you would have entire story and no location would be mentioned, no time would be mentioned.

171
00:15:26,544 --> 00:15:33,200
 In some stories you would have a time line, some stories you would have locations but its for a benefit.

172
00:15:34,371 --> 00:15:37,771
But these details are left out there is clear difference

173
00:15:38,050 --> 00:15:40,858
when you read a story in the Bible and when you read a story in Qur’an

174
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:43,558
it could be the same story but they are very different.

175
00:15:44,341 --> 00:15:50,045
The Bible gets into the name of the man, and his wife, and their fathers, and their relatives and their tribes

176
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:54,177
and who did this and who did that!

177
00:15:54,797 --> 00:16:01,541
 But the Qur’an goes straight into the story and mentions to you the just of it Al-Ibra(العبرة).

178
