353
00:29:41,277 --> 00:29:43,168
some said let's use this and let's use that.

354
00:29:44,073 --> 00:29:45,787
And then Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

355
00:29:50,081 --> 00:29:54,753
مُنْذُوْ نُوْأَرِّخُ مُنْذُوْ أَنْ خَرَجَ النَّبِيْ مِنْ الاَرْضِ شِّرْكْ

356
00:29:55,880 --> 00:30:00,424
Our calendar should start from the time Rasool Allah ﷺmade Hijrah(هجرة)

357
00:30:00,522 --> 00:30:06,338
 from the land of Shirk(شرك) to the land of Islam, the Hijrah(هجرة).

358
00:30:07,165 --> 00:30:11,765
So, it's interesting to see that, the Sahabah(صحابه) did not use for example, the birth of Rasool Allah ﷺ

359
00:30:12,650 --> 00:30:17,630
or his death or the date of his Prophet hood, they used Hijrah(هجرة).

360
00:30:18,216 --> 00:30:18,969
Why Hijrah(هجرة)?

361
00:30:19,842 --> 00:30:24,279
Why did they specifically choose Hijrah(هجرة), and didn’t choose his death or his birth.

362
00:30:24,934 --> 00:30:30,310
Well for his death Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) says, because that would bring bad memories.

363
00:30:33,021 --> 00:30:37,161
But then why didn’t they choose the date of his Prophet hood or the date of his birth?

364
00:30:37,273 --> 00:30:39,173
Why did they specifically choose date of Hijrah(الهجرة)?

365
00:30:39,325 --> 00:30:42,777
The Sahabah(صحابه) use to see the Hijrah(هجرة) is a turning point in Islam.

366
00:30:43,670 --> 00:30:45,503
 That is the beginning of Islamic State.

367
00:30:46,042 --> 00:30:49,114
That is the beginning of living a Islamic life.

368
00:30:50,394 --> 00:30:52,594
Before that we were a minority in Makkah.

369
00:30:53,117 --> 00:30:56,517
But now, we have an Ummah(امة) a nation

370
00:30:57,505 --> 00:31:02,705
and that’s why the Islamic Calendar should start from the Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

371
00:31:04,395 --> 00:31:09,539
So, that’s the year but the month, Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) in Rabia al-Awwal(ربيع الاول)

372
00:31:10,147 --> 00:31:12,731
however, the Islamic calendar starts with which month?

373
00:31:13,933 --> 00:31:15,245
What's the first month of the year?

374
00:31:15,697 --> 00:31:16,220
Muharram(محرم),

375
00:31:16,538 --> 00:31:18,007
Why did they choose Muharram(محرم)?

376
00:31:18,620 --> 00:31:21,036
One of the opinion and this is the opinion of Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) is

377
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:25,232
because Muharram(محرم) was the beginning of the intention of Rasool Allah ﷺ to make Hijrah(هجرة).

378
00:31:27,012 --> 00:31:30,212
Because Bai’at-Al-Aqabaa As-Saniya(بيعة العقبة الثانية), occurred in Zulhijah(ذوالحجة)

379
00:31:31,354 --> 00:31:36,398
and the first Hilal(هلال) after Zulhijah(ذوالحجة), the next month after Zulhijjah(ذوتاحجة) is Muharram(محرم).

380
00:31:39,927 --> 00:31:46,907
The other opinion is that it's good to start the year, after people come back from Hajj(حَجْ).

381
00:31:48,377 --> 00:31:54,377
So, people come back from Hajj(حَجْ) in Zulhijah(ذوالحجة) make that, the last month of the year

382
00:31:55,371 --> 00:31:59,035
and the people start off, the new year when they come back from Hajj(حَجْ).

383
00:32:00,976 --> 00:32:04,976
It could make a sense, Hajj(حَجْ) forgives for you, your sins

384
00:32:06,070 --> 00:32:13,324
and Umrah(عمرة) forgives the sins between Umrah(عمرة) and the next scenario starting again, in new month of Muharram(محرم).

385
00:32:13,937 --> 00:32:17,037
So, that’s how the Islamic Calendar started,

386
00:32:17,288 --> 00:32:22,188
it wasn’t something that was done in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ or the time of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

387
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:24,578
it was something that was started by Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

388
00:32:24,676 --> 00:32:28,522
So, you can see that when Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

389
00:32:29,474 --> 00:32:34,950
فَعَلَيْكُمْ بِسُنَّتِي وَسُنَّةِ الْخُلَفَاءِ الرَّاشِدِينَ الْمَهْدِيينَ، عَضُّوا عَلَيْهَا بِالنَّوَاجِذِ،

390
00:32:35,153 --> 00:32:42,533
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Follow my Sunnah(سنة) and the Sunnah(سنة) of the guided Caliphs after me.

391
00:32:44,253 --> 00:32:53,193
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that new affairs or circumstances would occur in the time of the Khulafah(خلافاء)

392
00:32:54,131 --> 00:32:58,843
and there will be some new rulings given by the Khulafah(خلافاء) and that needs to be taken as Sunnah(سنة).

393
00:33:00,212 --> 00:33:05,124
And many of these things occurred in the times of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

394
00:33:07,515 --> 00:33:11,483
There was another dilemma what to name the Khalifah(خليفه), what name to give him?

395
00:33:12,693 --> 00:33:15,690
With Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) he was given the name of,

396
00:33:16,034 --> 00:33:16,583
What?

397
00:33:17,161 --> 00:33:17,985
Khalifat(خليفة).

398
00:33:18,151 --> 00:33:19,023
Khalifat(خليفة) who?

399
00:33:19,795 --> 00:33:21,018
The successor of who?

400
00:33:22,330 --> 00:33:23,156
Khalifat(خليفة) who?

401
00:33:23,516 --> 00:33:24,708
Rasool Allah ﷺ,

402
00:33:25,124 --> 00:33:28,457
Khalifatu Rasool Allah(خليفة الرسول الله), that was the title of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) ,

403
00:33:29,397 --> 00:33:30,597
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

404
00:33:32,493 --> 00:33:34,465
 You cannot call me Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Ullah,

405
00:33:34,552 --> 00:33:36,552
I am not the Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Ullah, I am Khalifah(خليفه) of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

406
00:33:37,382 --> 00:33:38,749
 I am the successor of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

407
00:33:39,707 --> 00:33:43,419
So, if you give me the name Khalifat Khalifah(خليفه) tu Rasool Ullah,

408
00:33:43,681 --> 00:33:45,848
What about the ones who come after me?

409
00:33:45,923 --> 00:33:47,368
It going to become very, very long.

410
00:33:47,788 --> 00:33:50,526
Khalifat(خليفة), khalifat, khalifat ……. Rasool Ullah.

411
00:33:53,226 --> 00:33:57,390
So, they were thinking about a title to give the Khalifah(خليفه) and they couldn’t come up with one?

412
00:34:01,332 --> 00:34:07,650
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: He wants two competent men come down from Iraq,

413
00:34:07,754 --> 00:34:10,171
so that he can ask them about Iraq and its people.

414
00:34:10,883 --> 00:34:17,187
He wants to hold a meeting with men from Iraq to ask them about the conditions in Iraq.

415
00:34:17,699 --> 00:34:20,759
Iraq was a frontier land, there was a lot of fighting happening.

416
00:34:21,740 --> 00:34:23,740
So, he wanted to know the latest news.

417
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:29,588
So, they brought him the Lubaid Bin Rabi’a(لبيد ابن ربيعه) and Oda’e Bin Hatim(عدي بن حاتم).

418
00:34:32,637 --> 00:34:39,337
They came and they met Amro Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص)

419
00:34:40,953 --> 00:34:48,353
and they told Amro Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) can you please ask permission for us from Amir Ul Momineen(أميرالمؤمنين).

420
00:34:49,989 --> 00:34:51,921
Amro Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) he went to Umar(عُمَر) and he said;

421
00:34:52,069 --> 00:34:54,403
السلام و عليك يا امير المؤمنين

422
00:34:56,055 --> 00:34:57,455
السلام وعليكم يا امير المؤمنين

423
00:34:57,828 --> 00:34:59,628
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said, where did you get that from?

424
00:35:02,403 --> 00:35:06,003
Amro Bin Aas(عمرو بن العاص) told him; Lubaid Bin Rabi’a(لبيد ابن ربيعه) and Oda’e Bin Hatim(عدي بن حاتم) are outside

425
00:35:06,097 --> 00:35:09,161
and they said; we want permission to meet Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين)

426
00:35:09,543 --> 00:35:15,743
and I liked that name because we are the believers and you are our Ameer(امير).

427
00:35:17,716 --> 00:35:19,360
You are our Ameer(امير)!

428
00:35:20,058 --> 00:35:22,955
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "that would be the title"

429
00:35:23,217 --> 00:35:28,277
and since then Khulafah(خلافاء) were given the title of Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

430
00:35:38,899 --> 00:35:47,478
SOME OF THE QUALITIES OF AMEER UL-MOMINEEN(امير المؤمنين), Umar Ibn Al-Khattab Al Farooq رضي الله عنه,

431
00:35:49,374 --> 00:35:54,633
 He had such great fear of Allah in his heart,

432
00:35:55,549 --> 00:36:01,781
he had Khashiya Allah(خشية الله) and that's the fruit of knowledge, Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

433
00:36:02,099 --> 00:36:04,155
إِنَّمَا يَخْشَى اللَّهَ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْعُلَمَاءُ ۗ

434
00:36:04,550 --> 00:36:06,934
"The ones, who have fear of Allah are the Ulema(علماء)",

435
00:36:08,016 --> 00:36:09,349
so that’s the fruit of knowledge.

436
00:36:10,700 --> 00:36:17,796
The name of one man was mentioned in front of Imam Ahmad Bin Hanbal(امام احمدبن حنبل), so some of his students said;

437
00:36:18,424 --> 00:36:19,324
he is not a scholar.

438
00:36:19,815 --> 00:36:21,911
You know, they were putting him down, he doesn’t have Ilm(علم).

439
00:36:23,536 --> 00:36:25,372
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) responded and said;

440
00:36:26,215 --> 00:36:29,619
"He has the fruit of knowledge," the fear of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

441
00:36:31,002 --> 00:36:37,254
He already has the fruit of knowledge that is actually what you want knowledge to do for you,

442
00:36:38,192 --> 00:36:41,248
to have the fear of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and he had that.

443
00:36:42,945 --> 00:36:45,697
Anyway, with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he had the Khashiya(خشية) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

444
00:36:47,839 --> 00:36:50,487
Once a man came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

445
00:36:52,588 --> 00:36:59,732
and he said, O Umar(عُمَر)! I want you to solve this dispute happening between me and this man.

446
00:37:00,954 --> 00:37:02,958
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) became upset and he said,

447
00:37:03,280 --> 00:37:08,456
تَتْرُكُوْنَ عُمر وَهُوَ مُقْبِلٌ عَلَيْكُمْ حَتَّى اِذَاا شّتَغَلَ بِاَمُوْرِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ اَتَيْتُمُوْهَ

448
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:15,466
"When I come to you offering my help in my free time you don’t come forth

449
00:37:16,159 --> 00:37:20,015
and when you see me busy with the affairs of the Muslims, you rush to me

450
00:37:20,544 --> 00:37:21,907
and he hit him with his stick.

451
00:37:22,426 --> 00:37:24,006
The Durra(درة), the famous stick of Umar(عمر)

452
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:27,420
this is very famous stick, this is called Ad-Durra(ألدرة), the Durra(درة) of Umar(عمر).

453
00:37:29,903 --> 00:37:35,283
The man left and he was upset, he was complaining and he walked away.

454
00:37:37,276 --> 00:37:42,210
Sometimes, it happens that when you are free nobody comes to you

455
00:37:42,274 --> 00:37:45,856
and when all the paper work is piling up and you are so busy

456
00:37:46,110 --> 00:37:48,332
 everybody comes in with these urgent demands.

457
00:37:51,387 --> 00:37:52,891
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said; Call the man back.

458
00:37:54,206 --> 00:37:55,090
So, they called him.

459
00:37:55,749 --> 00:37:59,058
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) gave him the stick and he said;

460
00:37:59,291 --> 00:38:01,424
"I want you to hit me, like I hit you!"

461
00:38:04,310 --> 00:38:09,470
The man said: "For the sake of Allah and for your sake I won’t".

462
00:38:11,019 --> 00:38:12,291
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "No".

463
00:38:13,162 --> 00:38:17,702
You either do it, for the sake of Allah or you hit me back.

464
00:38:18,736 --> 00:38:21,304
Then the man said: I will do it, for the sake of Allah alone.

465
00:38:23,515 --> 00:38:26,091
Al-Ah'naf bin Qais(الاحنف بن قيس) said: "I was with Umar(عُمَر) when that happened.

466
00:38:26,265 --> 00:38:28,961
And he went into his house and we went with him and then he prayed

467
00:38:30,855 --> 00:38:32,963
and after he finished his Salah(صلاة), he said;

468
00:38:34,772 --> 00:38:42,196
يَا اِبْنِ الُخَطَابْ! كُنْتَ وَضِيْعًا فَرَفَعَكَ الله، وَكُنْتَ ضَالًا فَهَدَاـكَ الله ،

469
00:38:42,845 --> 00:38:45,045
وَكَنْتَ ذَلِيْلاً فَاعَزَّكَ الله،

470
00:38:46,329 --> 00:38:51,629
ثُمَّ حَمَلَكَ عَلى رِقَابِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ فَجَاءَكَ رَجُلٌ يَسْتَعْدِيْكَ فَضَرَبْتَه،

471
00:38:52,864 --> 00:38:55,408
مَاَ تَقُوْلُ لِرَبِّكَ غَدًا اِذَا اَتَيْتُه؟

472
00:38:57,106 --> 00:38:59,870
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said, O son of Khattab(خطاب), he is speaking to himself!

473
00:39:00,650 --> 00:39:06,952
He said: O son of Khattab(خطاب), You were low and Allah raised you,

474
00:39:08,047 --> 00:39:10,284
you were lost and Allah guided you,

475
00:39:11,251 --> 00:39:13,546
you were humble and Allah made you noble

476
00:39:14,475 --> 00:39:17,156
and then Allah appoints you over the Muslims,

477
00:39:17,660 --> 00:39:21,835
and a Muslim man comes to you asking for your help and you hit him.

478
00:39:22,966 --> 00:39:25,722
How will you answer to Allah on the Day you meet Him?

479
00:39:27,369 --> 00:39:32,069
What will you do and you will stand in front of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, how will you answer Allah for what you have done?

480
00:39:32,973 --> 00:39:36,629
Al-Ah'naf bin Qais(الاحنف بن قيس) said: When I saw that I knew the Umar(عُمَر) was the best of the men.

481
00:39:38,307 --> 00:39:44,059
This is the fear that he had, he regretted what he did with this man.

482
00:39:45,232 --> 00:39:50,655
Even though he was busy Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not see that he had the legitimate reason for doing what he did.

483
00:39:52,902 --> 00:39:54,210
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) used to say;

484
00:39:54,323 --> 00:39:56,123
حَاسِبُ اَنْفُسَكُمْ قَبْلَ اَنْ تُحَاسِبُ

485
00:39:57,512 --> 00:40:01,136
"Hold yourselves accountable before you will be held accountable."

486
00:40:02,599 --> 00:40:04,433
وَزِنُوْهَا قَبْلَ اَنْ تُوْزَنُوْا

487
00:40:04,619 --> 00:40:08,379
"And weigh yourselves on the scale, before you would be weighed."

488
00:40:09,556 --> 00:40:12,484
وَتَزَيَّنُوْا وَتَهَيَّئُوْ الِلْعَرْضِ الْأَكْبَرْ

489
00:40:13,025 --> 00:40:16,625
"And prepare yourselves for the great exposition."

490
00:40:17,646 --> 00:40:20,846
يَوْمَ تُعْرَضُوْنَ لَا تَخْفَى مِنْكُمْ خَافِيَةْ

491
00:40:20,925 --> 00:40:27,953
"The day you will be exposed and nothing will be hidden, prepare for that time, prepare for that day."

492
00:40:35,241 --> 00:40:43,517
Once Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) with his stick again, he hit men and women,

493
00:40:45,637 --> 00:40:50,613
who were making Wudhu(وضؤ) in a pool next to Al-Ka’aba(الكعبة) in Al-Haram(الحرم).

494
00:40:52,293 --> 00:40:56,985
So he hit them with his stick, he told them to go away.

495
00:40:58,354 --> 00:41:04,962
And then he called one of his employees, so the employee came and said;

496
00:41:05,082 --> 00:41:06,162
لَبَّيْكَ وَسَعْدَيْكََ

497
00:41:06,601 --> 00:41:09,249
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)" said: No lubayka(لبيك), No Sa’daiyka(سعديك)!"

498
00:41:10,126 --> 00:41:14,618
Didn’t I tell you to make separate pools for men and separate pools for women?

499
00:41:16,700 --> 00:41:18,820
Because they were making Wudhu(وضؤ) from the same pool

500
00:41:18,913 --> 00:41:22,853
 and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) didn’t want that mixing to occur next to the House of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

501
00:41:23,494 --> 00:41:24,616
So, he pushed them away.

502
00:41:25,918 --> 00:41:28,677
And then he told his employee why didn’t you follow my instructions?

503
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:35,002
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he went to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and he said:

504
00:41:35,050 --> 00:41:35,650
هَلَكْت

505
00:41:36,070 --> 00:41:37,110
"I perished!".

506
00:41:38,994 --> 00:41:41,282
 Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: "Why did you say that?"

507
00:41:41,875 --> 00:41:46,719
He said: "I hit men and women in the House of Allah in the Haram(حرم)".

508
00:41:49,181 --> 00:41:52,929
Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه said: "You are a shepherd

509
00:41:54,223 --> 00:41:59,419
and if the shepherd disciplines his flock then that is justice

510
00:42:00,213 --> 00:42:05,705
 but if the shepherd disciplines his flock wrongly then that is oppression!"

511
00:42:06,871 --> 00:42:11,031
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is saying you are a shepherd and you have a right to discipline

512
00:42:11,500 --> 00:42:13,500
 your flock when you see them doing wrong.

513
00:42:15,703 --> 00:42:22,787
Al-Hassan al-Basari(الحسن البصري) said, that one night while Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمربن الخطاب) was walking in the streets of Madina,

514
00:42:24,397 --> 00:42:26,431
he remembered the Ayah(آية).

515
00:42:26,491 --> 00:42:29,275
وَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْذُوْنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتْ

516
00:42:29,364 --> 00:42:33,596
The one's who harm, the believing men and the believing women,

517
00:42:35,704 --> 00:42:37,633
so he goes and visits Obaey Ibn Ka’aba(ابيئ ابن كعب),

518
00:42:37,696 --> 00:42:39,831
Obaey Ibn Ka’aba(ابيئ ابن كعب) was a scholar of Qur’an.

519
00:42:40,374 --> 00:42:44,510
He was one of the scribes, he was one of the memorizers of Book of Allah,

520
00:42:44,884 --> 00:42:48,808
he was one of the Mufassireen(مفسرين), so Umar(عُمَر) visits him.

521
00:42:51,033 --> 00:42:57,345
And as soon as he comes in to his house, Obaey Ibn Ka’aba(ابيئ ابن كعب) pulls down a pillow from beneath him

522
00:42:57,990 --> 00:42:59,326
and his gives it to the Khalifah(خليفه).

523
00:43:00,068 --> 00:43:03,964
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) kicks the pillow away and he sits down on the floor.

524
00:43:04,942 --> 00:43:12,086
And then he said: "Obaey(ابيئ) I fear that I am one of those, who are harming the believing men and the believing women."

525
00:43:14,293 --> 00:43:17,059
 Obaey Ibn Ka’aba رضي الله عنه told him.

526
00:43:18,878 --> 00:43:23,822
لَا تَسْتَطِيْعَ إِلَّا اَنْ تُعَاهِدْ رَعَيَّتَكْ فَتَأْمُرْ وَتَنْهَى

527
00:43:24,510 --> 00:43:31,538
O Umar(عُمَر)! You cannot but discipline your subjects and tell them what is right and what is wrong.

528
00:43:31,671 --> 00:43:34,931
You have to do that, you are the Khalifah(خليفه), Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

529
00:43:35,006 --> 00:43:36,218
قَدْ قُلْتَ وَاللهُ أَعْلَمْ،

530
00:43:36,725 --> 00:43:44,621
You have consoled me or you have comforted me, that's not the right translation really,

531
00:43:44,835 --> 00:43:45,783
قَدْ قُلْتَ وَاللهُ أَعْلَمْ،

532
00:43:45,877 --> 00:43:47,886
"You have said the right thing, you have said the right thing"!

533
00:43:48,700 --> 00:43:50,500
So Umar Ibn Khattab(عمرإبن خطاب) said: You said the right thing.

534
00:43:51,242 --> 00:43:57,194
But this shows you that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه used to have fear of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

535
00:43:57,245 --> 00:44:01,765
and he was so afraid that he would harm his subjects,

536
00:44:01,901 --> 00:44:05,817
he would harm someone and then he would be held accountable for that on the Day of Judgment.

537
00:44:05,946 --> 00:44:15,946
You know it's kind of difficult to make even a comparison between Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and some of the rulers of today.

538
00:44:16,669 --> 00:44:24,045
Who are using every way, that you can possibly think off to abuse, their followers

539
00:44:24,130 --> 00:44:29,378
and we are not talking about Kuffar(كفار) leaders, we are talking about the leaders in the Muslim world.

540
00:44:29,458 --> 00:44:31,578
May be they are Murtadeen(مرتدين), anyway, so it doesn’t make any difference.

541
00:44:32,183 --> 00:44:44,283
But I mean when you hear about their genius in the tools that they implement

542
00:44:44,918 --> 00:44:53,270
to torture the Awliya(اولياء) Allahعَزّوجَلّ, as I might have mentioned before, they would rape their family members.

543
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:59,444
They would use homosexuals against them, they would use sorcery, magic,

544
00:44:59,632 --> 00:45:05,208
they would actually hire magicians, hire sorcerers and fortune tellers, sorcerers and all different stuff,

545
00:45:05,975 --> 00:45:11,471
to cast magic spells on these Awliya(اولياء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

546
00:45:12,103 --> 00:45:23,767
They would use every psychological tool, that they could cast fear in their hearts, you name it.

547
00:45:24,581 --> 00:45:26,215
Physical abuse everything.

548
00:45:27,761 --> 00:45:29,861
 These rulers, they never think about Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

549
00:45:30,017 --> 00:45:34,065
they never think about the day, they will meet Allahعَزّوجَلّ and will be asked about what they're doing?

550
00:45:38,474 --> 00:45:42,974
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) sometimes when he would see fire, he would put his hand over it

551
00:45:44,701 --> 00:45:48,464
he would put his hand in the fire and he would say; "O son of Khattab(خطاب)!

552
00:45:50,350 --> 00:45:58,350
Can you have patience on this pain, is this a pain that you will be able to sustain? "

553
00:45:58,375 --> 00:45:59,355
he is telling himself.

554
00:46:00,602 --> 00:46:04,102
You need to be straight on Siraat-Ul-Mustaqeem(صراط المستقيم) when you are in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

555
00:46:04,205 --> 00:46:06,513
because this will be the consequence in Akhirah(آخرة), if you are not.

556
00:46:07,501 --> 00:46:12,713
And he would put his hand in fire and say; "Can you handle this? Son of Khattab(خطاب) can you handle this?".

557
00:46:16,749 --> 00:46:21,217
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was outstanding in his Zuhd(زهد), in his austerity.

558
00:46:22,949 --> 00:46:28,961
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was seen giving Khuttbah(خطبه) in a Thowb(ثوب) that had twelve patches.

559
00:46:30,673 --> 00:46:39,229
He was seen making Tawaf(طواف) in that thowb(ثوب).

560
00:46:40,295 --> 00:46:46,095
A Khalifah(خليفه), and he has twelve, stitches in his thowb(ثوب)

561
00:46:47,896 --> 00:46:52,680
and he wants to use it, until it's worn out completely before he gets a new one.

562
00:46:53,741 --> 00:46:54,941
And he is the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims.

563
00:46:57,428 --> 00:47:01,928
Hafsa(حفصه) his daughter, the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ  Umm-Al-Mo’mineen(ام المؤمنين) she came to him, and she said:

564
00:47:02,319 --> 00:47:03,519
اِنَّ الله اَكْثَرَ الْخَيْرَ

565
00:47:03,974 --> 00:47:11,246
وَ اَوْسَعَ عَلَيْكَ مِنَ الرِّزْقَ، فَلَوْأَكَلْتَ طَعَامًا أَطْيَبَ مِنْ ذَلِكْ وَلَبِسْتَ ثِيَابًاأَلْيَنَ مِنْ ثَوْبِكْ

566
00:47:12,690 --> 00:47:17,090
She told him, Allahعَزّوجَلّ has provided us with a lot of blessings

567
00:47:17,852 --> 00:47:21,028
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ has opened for us the doors of Rizq(رزق)

568
00:47:22,791 --> 00:47:25,795
 why don’t you get some better food and some better clothes?

569
00:47:26,879 --> 00:47:30,583
During the times of Rasool Ullah, there was poverty, may be in the time of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) there was poverty,

570
00:47:30,633 --> 00:47:32,333
but now we have Rizq(رزق) there is plenty.

571
00:47:33,175 --> 00:47:35,851
Why are you still following those strict rules of the past?

572
00:47:36,584 --> 00:47:38,788
 Why don’t you have some better food and some better clothes?

573
00:47:41,384 --> 00:47:44,584
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he looked at Hafsa(حفصه) and he said:

574
00:47:45,615 --> 00:47:47,815
"I want you to be the judge."

575
00:47:51,617 --> 00:47:57,845
And then he started reminding her with the way, Rasool Allah ﷺ used to live.

576
00:47:59,586 --> 00:48:07,326
And he went on, and on mentioning examples to her until, Hafsa(حفصه) started to cry and then Umar(عُمَر) said;

577
00:48:08,135 --> 00:48:14,503
 "I have two companions, who preceded me and I am going to follow this way of hardship,

578
00:48:15,780 --> 00:48:18,580
so that I can join them in the life of pleasure.

579
00:48:20,566 --> 00:48:26,542
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) they left before me and I want to follow them.

580
00:48:27,509 --> 00:48:31,365
And I am going to follow this way of hardship, this life style of difficulty.

581
00:48:31,966 --> 00:48:37,374
So, that I can join them in their life of happiness, this will be my way.

582
00:48:39,846 --> 00:48:43,146
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was not living for Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), he is living for the sake of

583
00:48:43,937 --> 00:48:49,505
 being reunited with his most beloved Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

584
00:48:54,550 --> 00:48:58,350
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he was once walking with his companions,

585
00:48:58,701 --> 00:49:06,805
advisors, deputies, came next to a dumpster, a garbage and he just stopped.

586
00:49:10,308 --> 00:49:12,274
فَكَأَنَّ اَصْحَابَه’ تَأَاذَّ وْا بِهَا

587
00:49:13,143 --> 00:49:19,643
"Until his companions were irritated because of the smell."

588
00:49:20,359 --> 00:49:28,359
This was a horribly stinking dump and they were getting irritated

589
00:49:29,170 --> 00:49:31,570
because he had them stand there for so long.

590
00:49:32,783 --> 00:49:34,883
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was trying to teach them a lesson.

591
00:49:36,614 --> 00:49:42,486
He said: This is your world, which you are fighting over and crying for.

592
00:49:43,733 --> 00:49:49,133
This is Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), this is what you are fighting over, this is it, it’s a stinking dumpster.

593
00:49:52,093 --> 00:49:55,909
And that is how Umar(عُمَر) saw this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), his interest was in Al-Akhirah(آخرة).

594
00:49:59,032 --> 00:50:01,052
Sa’ad Bin Abi Waqas رضي الله عنه, he said;

595
00:50:01,109 --> 00:50:03,793
وَاللهِ مَا كَانَ عُمر ابن الخطاب بِأَقْدَمِنَا هِجْرَةْ

596
00:50:03,952 --> 00:50:06,340
"Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was not the earliest among us in Hijrah(هجرة)."

597
00:50:07,591 --> 00:50:09,758
وَقَدْ عَرَفْتُ بِأَيِّ شَيْئٍ فَضَلَنَا

598
00:50:09,835 --> 00:50:15,979
"But I know how come Umar(عُمَر) is ahead of us! I know how come Umar(عُمَر) is better than us."

599
00:50:16,834 --> 00:50:21,834
كَانَأَازْهَدُنَا فِي الدُّنْيَاء

600
00:50:22,229 --> 00:50:25,705
He was the most austere among us.

601
00:50:26,570 --> 00:50:30,101
He was least attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) among all of us.

602
00:50:30,422 --> 00:50:35,630
That’s why Umar(عُمَر) stands above us, it is because of his Zuhd(زهد).

603
00:50:36,944 --> 00:50:45,920
The Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is right there in his hands and he leaves it, he discards it, he was very humble.

604
00:50:46,584 --> 00:50:48,304
TAWADHIA(تواضع) OF UMAR IBN KHATTAB(عمر ابن الخطاب)

605
00:50:48,890 --> 00:50:52,778
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was once approached by Al-Ahnaf Bin Qais(الاحنف بن قيس),

606
00:50:52,883 --> 00:50:55,991
Al-Ahnaf Bin Qais(الاحنف بن قيس) is one of the leaders of his people.

607
00:50:56,368 --> 00:51:04,244
A very dignified man, noble man he was respected by his community was loved and respected by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

608
00:51:04,950 --> 00:51:06,084
he was a chief of a tribe.

609
00:51:06,810 --> 00:51:08,402
 So, he came and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

610
00:51:08,442 --> 00:51:09,770
what was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) doing?

611
00:51:10,684 --> 00:51:21,252
The same thing he was doing when he was visited by Oyaiyna Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) applying Tor to his camel.

612
00:51:22,158 --> 00:51:28,634
Umar Ibn Khattab(عمرإبن خطاب) was applying Tor to his camel.

613
00:51:31,002 --> 00:51:37,250
And this is difficult job to do and it is something that is done by the slaves.

614
00:51:38,812 --> 00:51:41,696
You know, somebody who is well off he wouldn’t do that.

615
00:51:42,331 --> 00:51:48,319
You are applying this Tor to the camel to clear it from the flees.

616
00:51:49,011 --> 00:51:55,639
It's not something that should be done by somebody, who is a noble man let alone the Khalifah(خليفه).

617
00:51:56,641 --> 00:51:58,473
But that’s what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was doing.

618
00:51:59,699 --> 00:52:03,935
And it's very difficult thing to do, so you have to take your clothes off.

619
00:52:07,240 --> 00:52:09,940
 So, Al-Ahnaf(الاحنف) came, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him:

620
00:52:09,997 --> 00:52:12,409
O Ahnaf(احنف) take your clothes off and come and join me.

621
00:52:13,872 --> 00:52:16,672
Obviously when he said, take your clothes off, it means the outer garment,

622
00:52:17,034 --> 00:52:21,846
you have your inner clothes that would cover your body on.

623
00:52:22,058 --> 00:52:27,258
But your clean clothes that you wear when you outside take those out

624
00:52:27,491 --> 00:52:29,391
because you are dealing with Tor, Qataraan(قطران).

625
00:52:35,853 --> 00:52:41,985
So, there is one man with them he said: O Umar(عُمَر) Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين)!

626
00:52:42,482 --> 00:52:46,998
Why don’t you have, a slave do that? Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) responded by saying;

627
00:52:47,044 --> 00:52:50,900
وَأَيُّ عَبْدٍ هُوَّ أَعْبَدْ مِنِّيْ وَمِنَّ الْأحنف؟

628
00:52:52,149 --> 00:52:55,861
"And who is more of a slave then me and Al-Ahnaf(الاحنف)?"

629
00:52:56,618 --> 00:53:04,618
إِنَّه’ مَنْ وَلِيَ اَمْرُالْمُسْلِمِيْنَ، يَجِبْ عَلَيْهِ لَهُمْ مَا يَجِبُ عَلَى الْعَبْدِ لِسَيِّدِهْ فِيْ فِى النَّصِيْحَةْ وَأَدَاءِالْأَمَانَهْ

630
00:53:05,565 --> 00:53:07,841
 "And who is more of a slave then me and Al-Ahnaf(الاحنف)?

631
00:53:08,288 --> 00:53:16,576
Anyone who assumes responsibility over the Muslims is accountable just like the slave is accountable to his master."

632
00:53:18,902 --> 00:53:22,902
And he is talking about the fact that he is accountable to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

633
00:53:23,557 --> 00:53:28,577
He is a slave and Al-Ahnaf(الاحنف) is a slave and they are appointed over the Muslims,

634
00:53:29,184 --> 00:53:32,744
so they need to be accountable to their Master, Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

635
00:53:33,484 --> 00:53:39,904
Just because I am your leader shouldn’t make you forget that I am still a slave

636
00:53:39,996 --> 00:53:42,916
and that I have a Master above me, Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

637
00:53:45,963 --> 00:53:47,497
In a gathering some man said,

638
00:53:48,666 --> 00:53:51,866
مَا رَأَيْنَا رَجًلً أَقْضَى بِلْحَقِّ بِالْقِسْطِ

639
00:53:53,737 --> 00:53:58,637
وَلَاأَاقْوَلَ لِلْحَقِّ وَلَاأَاشَّدَّ عَلَى الْمُنَافِقِيْنَ مِنْكَ يا امير المؤمنين

640
00:54:01,395 --> 00:54:05,899
فَأَنْتَ خَيْرُا النَّاسِ بَعْدَ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

641
00:54:08,401 --> 00:54:15,701
They said: We had never seen anyone, who is more just and who says, speaks the truth

642
00:54:16,564 --> 00:54:21,104
and who is more severe on the Munafiqeen(منافقين) then you?

643
00:54:22,605 --> 00:54:25,553
Auf Bin Malik(عوف بن مالك) who was sitting there he said: No! that's not true.

644
00:54:25,610 --> 00:54:26,710
Kazabtu(كذبت), you are lying.

645
00:54:27,743 --> 00:54:34,607
And then he said, we know of somebody, who came after Rasool Allah ﷺ who is better than Umar(عُمَر).

646
00:54:35,879 --> 00:54:37,779
And this was said in front of Umar(عُمَر).

647
00:54:39,281 --> 00:54:42,625
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: "Who are you talking about?"

648
00:54:45,607 --> 00:54:47,355
He said: "I am talking about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)",

649
00:54:48,432 --> 00:54:51,116
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You are right.!

650
00:54:52,350 --> 00:54:57,550
There was a time when Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكر الصديق) was more pure then musk(مسك)

651
00:54:58,869 --> 00:55:02,817
and I was more mislead then the camel of my parents.

652
00:55:04,982 --> 00:55:08,766
I was in a worse condition then the camel of my family.

653
00:55:09,194 --> 00:55:12,422
While Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه his smell was better than musk(مسك).

654
00:55:13,335 --> 00:55:16,351
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was saying that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) became Muslim before me

655
00:55:17,234 --> 00:55:19,066
and he was pure and clean like musk(مسك),

656
00:55:19,489 --> 00:55:24,169
while I was a disbeliever and I was worse than the camel of my family.

657
00:55:25,870 --> 00:55:29,270
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wasn't insulted by what this man said,

658
00:55:29,621 --> 00:55:33,450
when he said that you are not the best after Rasool Allah ﷺ.

659
00:55:33,717 --> 00:55:37,001
Umar(عُمَر) wanted the people to know who he really is?

660
00:55:37,432 --> 00:55:40,912
And that he is in lower status than Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

661
00:55:42,351 --> 00:55:47,495
He didn’t allow the people to tempt him, to believe that he is better

662
00:55:47,756 --> 00:55:51,276
like people, the deceptive people do today to leaders.

663
00:55:52,030 --> 00:55:55,298
They deceive the leaders and make them think that they are better than everybody else.

664
00:55:56,024 --> 00:56:00,576
You are the best king that ever existed in history, you are the best leader that ever lived.

665
00:56:00,757 --> 00:56:02,323
You are the best president, whatever!

666
00:56:03,684 --> 00:56:04,484
And they pumped them up

667
00:56:05,393 --> 00:56:09,937
and it gets to you, after a while it gets into your brains, and you really think that I am the best.

668
00:56:12,630 --> 00:56:14,050
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) did not allow that.

669
00:56:14,788 --> 00:56:20,668
And he had, in his presence people, who would not allow that, like ‘Awf bin Malik(عوف بن مالك).

670
00:56:29,687 --> 00:56:36,387
And HE WAS ALSO FOREBEARING:

671
00:56:36,594 --> 00:56:42,066
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه even though he had that strong personality but he had Helm(حلم).

672
00:56:43,032 --> 00:56:46,008
Oyaiyna Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) again, his name comes up,

673
00:56:46,575 --> 00:56:47,875
he is the Bedouin leader

674
00:56:48,943 --> 00:56:55,070
whom Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) tore the document that was given by Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he tore it apart.

675
00:56:55,608 --> 00:56:59,408
Oyaiyna Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) wanted permission to meet with Umar(عُمَر)

676
00:56:59,814 --> 00:57:03,414
because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) would surround himself as Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) says;

677
00:57:03,957 --> 00:57:05,691
With the scholars of Qur’an.

678
00:57:07,730 --> 00:57:12,794
These would be his advisors let's say.

679
00:57:15,650 --> 00:57:17,317
They were friends and also advisors.

680
00:57:17,582 --> 00:57:20,530
These are the people with whom he would surround himself with the Bataana(بطانه).

681
00:57:23,464 --> 00:57:27,156
And Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said, it doesn’t matter whether they were old or young

682
00:57:27,287 --> 00:57:32,059
 as long as they were scholars in Qur’an they understood Qur’an they would accompany Umar(عُمَر).

683
00:57:33,621 --> 00:57:36,315
So, one of them is Al-Hurr Bin Qais(الحر بن قيس).

684
00:57:37,887 --> 00:57:39,359
Oyaiyna Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن) was his uncle.

685
00:57:39,919 --> 00:57:42,039
So, Oyaiyna(عيينه) is coming to Al-Hurr(الحر) and said:

686
00:57:42,328 --> 00:57:46,412
 I want you to arrange a meeting between me and Umar(عُمَر), I want to meet him.

687
00:57:47,181 --> 00:57:51,381
So, Al-Hurr Bin Qais(الحر بن قيس), because he is very close to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he asked Umar(عُمَر)

688
00:57:51,999 --> 00:57:55,399
for permission to have ‘Oyaiyna(عيينه) come in.

689
00:57:56,179 --> 00:57:57,295
So, Umar(عُمَر) allowed him in.

690
00:57:57,606 --> 00:57:59,907
Oyaiyna(عيينه) comes in and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) look at what he said;

691
00:58:00,813 --> 00:58:01,410
He said;

692
00:58:03,140 --> 00:58:07,420
هِيْ يا ابن الخطاب فَوَالله مَا تُعْطِيْنَا الْجَزْلَ وَلَا تَحْكُمْ فِيْنَا بِالْعَدْلَ

693
00:58:08,579 --> 00:58:13,943
"O son of Khattab(خطاب)! You are not giving us enough and you are not judging among us with justice.

694
00:58:15,798 --> 00:58:18,538
"You are being oppressive and you are not giving us enough.

695
00:58:18,955 --> 00:58:23,095
And you really need to look at the first statement, you are not giving us enough that’s what it really means.

696
00:58:23,564 --> 00:58:27,088
And Umar(عُمَر) is oppressive because he is not giving him enough.

697
00:58:27,837 --> 00:58:33,177
 So, you know sometimes people their standard of justice is how good you are to them.

698
00:58:34,068 --> 00:58:38,524
 That is, they see the world, they are the centre of universe.

699
00:58:39,811 --> 00:58:44,611
If you treat them well then you are the best, if you treat them bad, you are the worst.

700
00:58:45,571 --> 00:58:51,295
Doesn’t really make a difference whether they have merits or not.

701
00:58:51,733 --> 00:58:53,933
They judge according to how they are treated.

702
00:58:56,591 --> 00:59:02,219
 And this is a statement that is false, so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to respond back.

703
00:59:03,746 --> 00:59:09,946
Al-Hurr Bin Qais(الحر بن قيس) interrupted and he said, Allahعَزّوجَلّ has told Muhammad  ﷺ,

704
00:59:10,409 --> 00:59:12,009
وَاَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجَاهِلِيْنِ

705
00:59:12,705 --> 00:59:15,745
"Stay away from the ignorant and this man is one of them."

706
00:59:16,707 --> 00:59:23,219
He is saying that about his uncle, but Al-Hurr Bin Qais(الحر بن قيس) defends Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه

707
00:59:23,602 --> 00:59:24,911
 because he is defending the truth.

708
00:59:25,323 --> 00:59:27,823
Even if that leads to him insulting his own uncle.

709
00:59:27,908 --> 00:59:31,232
 This man is among Al-Jahiliyeen(الجاهلين) and the Ayah(آية) says,

710
00:59:31,321 --> 00:59:32,521
وَاَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجَاهِلِيْنِ

711
00:59:32,587 --> 00:59:35,159
stay away from them. Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said,

712
00:59:35,766 --> 00:59:37,933
فَمَا تَجَاوَزَهَا حِيْنَ تَلَاهَا

713
00:59:38,131 --> 00:59:42,819
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) didn’t go beyond that as soon as the verse was revealed.

714
00:59:43,118 --> 00:59:45,118
فَاِنَّه’ كَانَ وَقَافًا عِنْدَ كِتَابِ الله

715
00:59:45,442 --> 00:59:48,450
"Because Umar(عُمَر) was a person who would stop at the Book of Allah."

716
00:59:49,862 --> 00:59:52,006
When he would hear a Ayah(آية) he would stop.

717
00:59:52,701 --> 00:59:57,244
He would follow the rule of Allahعَزّوجَلّ he would not go ahead with what he intended

718
00:59:57,654 --> 01:00:02,202
because now he heard a Naseeha(نصيحه) the Ayah(آية) of the Book of Allahعَزّوجَلّ telling him to ignore.

719
01:00:02,363 --> 01:00:03,839
So, he ignored Oyaiyna Bin Hassan(عيينه بن حصن).

720
01:00:13,579 --> 01:00:16,313
Lets move on to the  other section,

721
01:00:17,031 --> 01:00:20,811
HIS LIFE WITH HIS FAMILY:

722
01:00:24,710 --> 01:00:28,406
Rasool Allah ﷺ was in a gathering with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

723
01:00:29,468 --> 01:00:37,900
and Rasool Allah ﷺ would use various instructional methods to deliver the message to the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

724
01:00:38,685 --> 01:00:43,161
For example, sometimes he would draw a diagram on the sand,

725
01:00:43,795 --> 01:00:45,528
 sometimes he would ask a question,

726
01:00:47,291 --> 01:00:57,327
sometimes he would make a statement like an oath to make them attentive, to what he's going to say

727
01:00:58,675 --> 01:01:02,975
and the statements of Rasool Allah ﷺ were very short and concise, so that they could be remembered.

728
01:01:04,115 --> 01:01:08,315
So, all of these show you the Hikmah(حكمة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ as a Teacher.

729
01:01:10,124 --> 01:01:13,668
Once Rasool Allah ﷺ was with the Sahabah(صحابه), so he asked them a question.

730
01:01:13,798 --> 01:01:18,162
He said: "Tell me what tree is similar to the Mo’min(مؤمن), to the believer?

731
01:01:20,293 --> 01:01:23,109
" Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) said; I was with the Sahabah(صحابه).

732
01:01:25,083 --> 01:01:28,475
And the Sahabah(صحابه) got lost in the trees of the desert.

733
01:01:29,087 --> 01:01:35,383
The Sahabah(صحابه), their minds tuned in to the desert and they started mentioning names of tree from the desert.

734
01:01:36,513 --> 01:01:40,617
While the tree Rasool Allah ﷺ was referring to right to, was right around the corner.

735
01:01:42,808 --> 01:01:47,032
Rasool Allah ﷺ was referring to An-Nakhla(النخلة), the palm tree.

736
01:01:49,661 --> 01:02:00,201
Since, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم went around mentioning one tree after another, none of them knew the answer.

737
01:02:00,332 --> 01:02:03,900
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them the answer. He said: It is An-Nakhla(النخلة), the palm tree.

738
01:02:05,709 --> 01:02:09,513
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) he went back home and he told his father, O my father! I knew the answer.

739
01:02:11,146 --> 01:02:13,766
Umar(عُمَر) told him, "why didn’t you answer it then?"

740
01:02:14,973 --> 01:02:19,905
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) said: "Because I was the youngest in the gathering

741
01:02:20,214 --> 01:02:24,998
and there were people like you and Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), so I was shy, embarrassed.

742
01:02:26,292 --> 01:02:29,984
I didn’t feel it right to answer in their presence."

743
01:02:31,248 --> 01:02:33,820
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) didn’t like that answer, and he said;

744
01:02:34,840 --> 01:02:38,540
 "It would have been better if you have answered

745
01:02:38,942 --> 01:02:43,474
and I would rather, that have you answer that question Bikadhaa(بكذا) Wa-kadhaa(وكذاء),

746
01:02:43,733 --> 01:02:45,733
this was a statement what they would say meaning,

747
01:02:47,259 --> 01:02:52,023
 "Whatever you could sacrifice, it would have been better for me, if you mentioned the answer then."

748
01:02:53,556 --> 01:02:58,024
What Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is teaching his son Abdullah(عبدالله) is that you should have courage.

749
01:02:59,209 --> 01:03:02,653
You should speak up, when you know the truth.

750
01:03:03,431 --> 01:03:06,207
You shouldn’t just stay there quietly because you are shy,

751
01:03:06,725 --> 01:03:08,809
because you don’t want to talk in front of the gathering

752
01:03:09,722 --> 01:03:12,922
and this is very important message to deliver it to your children.

753
01:03:13,583 --> 01:03:18,583
Don’t be shy, don’t be ashamed if you know the right answer, you know the truth, answer it.

754
01:03:19,247 --> 01:03:21,547
So, he is teaching his son Abdullah(عبدالله) to have courage

755
01:03:22,811 --> 01:03:25,411
and this is an important thing that we need to teach our children.

756
01:03:26,819 --> 01:03:33,219
In fact, sometimes parents would teach their children fear, not courage, fear.

757
01:03:33,833 --> 01:03:40,633
Stay away from trouble, don’t answer, don’t talk, don’t speak up, don’t go to the Masjid(مسجد), don’t do this, don’t do that.

758
01:03:43,473 --> 01:03:49,225
You should tell them, that they should uphold the truth no matter what the consequences are.

759
01:03:50,625 --> 01:03:54,725
You should stand up for what is right no matter what the consequences are.

760
01:03:55,153 --> 01:04:00,337
Parents do not make your children grow up to be chicken.

761
01:04:02,597 --> 01:04:11,897
You need to raise them up having the Ikhlaq(اخلاق) of Islam, courage, sacrifice.

762
01:04:13,197 --> 01:04:15,889
Ibrahim عليه السّلام is telling his son I want to slaughter you?

763
01:04:16,093 --> 01:04:20,057
What do you say? Because he was brought up by Ibrahim عليه السّلام, he said,

764
01:04:20,147 --> 01:04:21,147
يَا أَبَتِ افْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ

765
01:04:21,304 --> 01:04:23,704
O my father do what you are commanded to do.

766
01:04:25,284 --> 01:04:29,268
He was ready, Ismailعليه السلام was ready to die for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

767
01:04:31,821 --> 01:04:38,501
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) use to care for, the Akhirah(آخرة) benefit for his children.

768
01:04:39,374 --> 01:04:43,807
When Hafsa(حفصه), her husband died.

769
01:04:46,170 --> 01:04:48,558
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted her to marry the best.

770
01:04:51,383 --> 01:04:52,955
So, he goes to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان).

771
01:04:53,544 --> 01:04:59,284
 I want fathers, I want parents in general, fathers and mothers to think about this.

772
01:04:59,613 --> 01:05:04,141
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) goes to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

773
01:05:05,584 --> 01:05:14,168
and he tells him, my daughter Hafsa(حفصه), I am offering her to you in marriage.

774
01:05:16,666 --> 01:05:20,366
This is no, no to parents today, you don’t go offering your daughter around.

775
01:05:21,563 --> 01:05:27,579
You wait until somebody comes, and if nobody comes you have her sit at home, until she dies.

776
01:05:29,724 --> 01:05:33,288
 No Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he wants the best for his daughter.

777
01:05:33,989 --> 01:05:37,870
He is not thinking about shame, embarrassment and he doesn’t think about these things.

778
01:05:38,992 --> 01:05:43,188
I want her benefit, I want what is good for her, so he goes to Uthman(عثمان) and he says;

779
01:05:43,302 --> 01:05:44,846
 "I am offering you my daughter in marriage".

780
01:05:47,008 --> 01:05:48,960
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) comes back to Umar(عُمَر) and says;

781
01:05:49,036 --> 01:05:52,360
قَدْ بَدَلِيْ اَلَّا تَزَوَّجَ فِيْ يَوْمِ هَذَا اَوْ يَوْمِ هَذَا

782
01:05:52,812 --> 01:05:56,824
I am not interested in marrying, at this particular time.

783
01:05:59,382 --> 01:06:00,682
Umar(عُمَر) didn’t like that answer.

784
01:06:01,341 --> 01:06:03,753
 Obviously, but you cannot force him.

785
01:06:04,755 --> 01:06:07,828
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) turned him down, it's very difficult.

786
01:06:08,574 --> 01:06:12,422
but Uthman(عثمان) wasn’t interested in getting married at that particular time.

787
01:06:15,074 --> 01:06:20,574
So, then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he goes to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and he offers Hafsa(حفصه) to him.

788
01:06:22,888 --> 01:06:27,224
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكر الصديق) did not respond back, he did not say, yes or no. He just left.

789
01:06:28,556 --> 01:06:31,356
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said; And I was even more upset with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

790
01:06:31,682 --> 01:06:33,291
at least Uthman(عثمان) told me the answer.

791
01:06:33,466 --> 01:06:35,674
He said, No!. Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) just ignored me.

792
01:06:39,282 --> 01:06:42,282
So Umar Ibn Khattab(عمرإبن ألخطاب) was very angry with Abu Bakr(أبوبكر), very angry.

793
01:06:48,982 --> 01:06:59,130
A short while later, Rasool Allah ﷺ asks for Hafsa(حفصه) and he marries her, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

794
01:07:00,602 --> 01:07:08,954
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) comes back to Umar(عُمَر) and he said: "I think you were upset with me?

795
01:07:10,408 --> 01:07:11,513
" Umar(عُمَر) said: "Yes".

796
01:07:12,227 --> 01:07:24,675
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: The reason why I didn’t answer back is because I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ mention her name,

797
01:07:26,521 --> 01:07:31,621
and I am not going to be the one, to expose the secret of Rasool Allah ﷺ

798
01:07:33,168 --> 01:07:37,268
and if Rasool Allah ﷺ did not get marry to her, I would have married her.

799
01:07:39,052 --> 01:07:44,052
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said; It was something I heard in private, and I wouldn't tell anybody about it.

800
01:07:45,664 --> 01:07:50,664
Rasool Ullah mentioned her name, so I wanted to wait and see if Rasool Allah ﷺ would marry her.

801
01:07:51,221 --> 01:07:53,321
And if he didn’t, I would have married her.

802
01:07:54,289 --> 01:07:58,645
But Allahعَزّوجَلّ chose for her the best, Muhammadﷺ.

803
01:08:01,139 --> 01:08:04,839
But the thing here is, we are talking about how he is dealing with his family.

804
01:08:05,365 --> 01:08:11,765
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is eager to get the best husband for his daughter

805
01:08:12,112 --> 01:08:13,979
and he is willing to go and offer her.

806
01:08:21,359 --> 01:08:23,703
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was strict with his family members.

807
01:08:24,748 --> 01:08:31,328
And when he was a Khalifah(خليفه), he wanted to make sure that there is no favoritism going on,

808
01:08:33,897 --> 01:08:35,263
and he was very strict about it.

809
01:08:36,277 --> 01:08:45,997
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) said; I purchased some camels that were very weak because of fever.

810
01:08:46,772 --> 01:08:51,406
These camels were sick, so they became very weak, skinny

811
01:08:53,390 --> 01:08:57,936
Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) purchased them and then he took them to Al-Hima(الهِما).

812
01:08:58,011 --> 01:09:05,031
Al-Hima(الهِما) is a guarded area that is open for all, it is a common pasture.

813
01:09:05,767 --> 01:09:08,023
So, the land doesn’t belong to any particular person.

814
01:09:08,344 --> 01:09:13,404
It is guarded and any Muslim can take their flock there to feed.

815
01:09:14,426 --> 01:09:20,762
So, Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) he took his camels to this Hima(الهِما) and they grew fat

816
01:09:21,568 --> 01:09:24,036
and then Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) took them to the market place to sell.

817
01:09:25,003 --> 01:09:29,931
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he used to inspect the markets of Madina.

818
01:09:30,645 --> 01:09:38,345
So, during one of his inspections tours, he sees these fat healthy camels.

819
01:09:38,661 --> 01:09:40,694
He said, who did these belongs to?

820
01:09:41,180 --> 01:09:42,904
They said; They belonged to Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر).

821
01:09:44,250 --> 01:09:49,458
So, he calls Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) and he said; O Abdullah(عبدالله) what is this?

822
01:09:50,935 --> 01:09:54,427
Abdullah(عبدالله) said; These are some camels I bought, they were very skinny

823
01:09:54,509 --> 01:09:58,413
and I took them to Hima(الهِما) and now I want to sell them.

824
01:09:59,783 --> 01:10:04,523
Umar(عُمَر) said; Yes!. You took them to Hima(الهِما) and the Muslims over there said;

825
01:10:05,605 --> 01:10:13,445
Move away let the camels of the son of Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين) eat and they would bring them water

826
01:10:13,678 --> 01:10:18,254
and say take good care of the camels of the son of Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين), until they grew fat.

827
01:10:20,491 --> 01:10:27,343
Sell these camels, you take your capital and every single Dinar(دينار), you made in profit goes back to the treasury.

828
01:10:30,138 --> 01:10:33,094
Because Umar(عُمَر) said that, because you are the son of the Khalifah(خليفه),

829
01:10:34,364 --> 01:10:40,332
the Muslims were giving you preferred treatment and that’s why your camels became fat.

830
01:10:42,592 --> 01:10:47,196
So, he said, you take your capital the money that you have invested and don’t make money any money out of this.

831
01:10:52,010 --> 01:10:59,310
Abdullah Ibn Umar رضي الله عنه, he made some money from the Ghanaem(غنائم) of the Jalolah(جوالاء) this was the battle in Iraq.

832
01:11:00,049 --> 01:11:08,569
So, Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) being one of the fighter in the army, he got portion of the spoils of war.

833
01:11:09,209 --> 01:11:12,365
So, he brought it to Madina and he wanted to sell it.

834
01:11:13,788 --> 01:11:23,568
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said; "Yes". You going to sell it, you are going to make a lot of money off, of it.

835
01:11:24,344 --> 01:11:34,244
Actually, it cost him 40,000 and he sold it for four hundred thousand (400,000), so he made a lot of money.

836
01:11:34,295 --> 01:11:35,275
It was a very good deal.

837
01:11:39,482 --> 01:11:44,586
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه said; O my son Abdullah(عبدالله)!

838
01:11:46,685 --> 01:11:52,237
Would you sacrifice any thing for me, if you know that you are father is going to hellfire?

839
01:11:53,367 --> 01:11:57,079
Abdullah(عبدالله) said; O my father! I would sacrifice anything for you, anything.

840
01:11:58,389 --> 01:12:05,989
Umar(عُمَر) said, well this merchandise of yours, which you want to sell, the Muslims are going to say,

841
01:12:07,225 --> 01:12:15,033
he is the Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Ullah and he is the son of Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين)

842
01:12:16,639 --> 01:12:22,699
and he the most beloved of his sons to him and then Umar(عُمَر) said, and that is true.

843
01:12:23,966 --> 01:12:26,730
Umar(عُمَر) was saying, that you are the most beloved of my children to me.

844
01:12:28,270 --> 01:12:32,026
So, the Muslims are going to give you the best deal.

845
01:12:33,826 --> 01:12:39,690
They are going to sell you with the lower prices and they will buy from you with the highest prices.

846
01:12:41,496 --> 01:12:47,896
So, let me tell you my son, I am going to give you best profit a man of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) can make.

847
01:12:48,990 --> 01:12:52,630
For every Dirham(درهم) that you have invested I am going to give you a Dirham(درهم).

848
01:12:54,505 --> 01:12:59,005
So, after it was sold for four hundred thousand,

849
01:12:59,697 --> 01:13:03,597
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) gave Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) Eighty Thousand(80,000)

850
01:13:04,357 --> 01:13:06,553
 all of the rest went to Bait-Ul-Maal(بيت المال), the treasury.

851
01:13:09,247 --> 01:13:12,871
Now, this is a legitimate deal but Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very sensitive,

852
01:13:13,412 --> 01:13:15,540
very sensitive to the way, his son would be treated.

853
01:13:17,975 --> 01:13:25,375
In fact Abdullah(عبدالله) and Ubaidillah Bin Umar(عبيدالله بن عمر) were in Iraq,

854
01:13:26,162 --> 01:13:27,790
they were with Abu Musa Al-Asha’ari(ابوموسى العشعري)

855
01:13:29,549 --> 01:13:34,197
and Abu Musa Al-Asha’ari(ابوموسى العشعري) is appointed as a Governor by Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

856
01:13:34,851 --> 01:13:38,507
So Abu Musa(ابوموسى) told Abdullah(عبدالله) and Ubaidillah(عبيدالله ), he said;

857
01:13:39,079 --> 01:13:41,243
 I want to send some money to the Khalifah(خليفه).

858
01:13:41,603 --> 01:13:43,635
I want to send some money to Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

859
01:13:46,262 --> 01:13:55,486
However, I am going to give you this money, you buy some items from Iraq, using this money

860
01:13:56,670 --> 01:14:02,570
and you can take it to Madina and sell it and give the money back to Umar(عُمَر) and you keep the profit.

861
01:14:04,055 --> 01:14:05,055
So, you see the deal here?

862
01:14:06,539 --> 01:14:10,187
So, Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عُمَر) took the money that belongs to Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين),

863
01:14:10,534 --> 01:14:13,950
should go back to the treasury and they bought some items from Iraq,

864
01:14:14,154 --> 01:14:18,186
they carried the items and they wanted to sell them in Madina.

865
01:14:19,848 --> 01:14:24,596
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) when he knew about this deal he said: No.

866
01:14:25,319 --> 01:14:34,891
He said, all of the money goes to the treasury.

867
01:14:36,468 --> 01:14:40,800
Abdullah(عبدالله) said, I stayed, quiet and Ubaidillah(عبيدالله) argued with my father.

868
01:14:40,887 --> 01:14:52,559
He said; But my father, if we lost in this deal we would have guaranteed the return of the money.

869
01:14:53,825 --> 01:14:56,905
So, how come now when we made money you want to take it away from us?

870
01:14:57,900 --> 01:15:02,800
Because if this turned out to be a sour deal, we would have paid you money out of our pockets

871
01:15:03,712 --> 01:15:05,604
because this was a trust given by Abu Musa(ابوموسى).

872
01:15:06,675 --> 01:15:09,375
Umar(عُمَر) said; Give the money back.

873
01:15:11,012 --> 01:15:17,144
So, one of the Sahabah(صحابه) was sitting there he argued on behalf of Abdullah(عبدالله) and Ubaidillah(عبيدالله) and he said,

874
01:15:17,770 --> 01:15:24,706
O Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين) how about you give them half of the profit and you take half?

875
01:15:25,250 --> 01:15:29,382
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he remained silent, so that's what happened.

876
01:15:33,962 --> 01:15:43,906
His son Asim(عاصم) was in Iraq and he came with some plates and jewelry, and

877
01:15:44,693 --> 01:15:45,960
some items that he brought them from Iraq.

878
01:15:47,092 --> 01:15:51,672
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) called Mo’aiqeeb(موعيقيب) his servant and he said;

879
01:15:51,771 --> 01:15:58,623
 Mo’aiqeeb(موعيقيب) take everything you see with Asim(عاصم) and deposit it in the treasury.

880
01:15:59,409 --> 01:16:05,633
Asim(عاصم) said: But it belongs to me. Umar(عُمَر) said: No! You went to Iraq and you asked them to give you this.

881
01:16:07,017 --> 01:16:09,017
Asim(عاصم) said; But I asked my family.

882
01:16:09,974 --> 01:16:15,098
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told Mo'aiqeeb(موعيقيب) take it, and leave it in treasury, take it all.

883
01:16:15,376 --> 01:16:19,808
And he Stripped Asim(عاصم) of all of the items that he brought with him from Iraq and he put it in the treasury.

884
01:16:23,037 --> 01:16:33,437
Abu Musa Al-Asha’ari(ابوموسى العشعري) he came from Iraq and he gave the wife of Umar(عُمَر) a gift.

885
01:16:36,160 --> 01:16:40,180
Small item, he gave to her as a gift to wife of Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

886
01:16:41,821 --> 01:16:48,073
Umar(عُمَر) comes in and he sees this gift with his wife he said; where did you get it from?

887
01:16:48,517 --> 01:16:50,853
She said; Abu Musa Al-Asha’ari(ابوموسى العشعري) gave it to me, as a gift.

888
01:16:51,747 --> 01:16:58,919
Umar(عُمَر) picked up that item and he hit her on the head, he banged her on her head and he said;

889
01:16:59,156 --> 01:17:02,976
and why are you getting gifts from Abu Musa(ابوموسى)?

890
01:17:04,361 --> 01:17:05,361
And then he said; call Abu Musa(ابوموسى).

891
01:17:06,803 --> 01:17:13,995
Abu Musa(ابوموسى) came in and he was breathing, because they had dragged him and he had to run he said;

892
01:17:14,172 --> 01:17:15,905
لَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيَّا يا امير المؤمنين

893
01:17:15,969 --> 01:17:18,425
O Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين), Don’t hasten in your judgment against me.

894
01:17:18,809 --> 01:17:21,757
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him, and who told you give my wife gifts?

895
01:17:23,117 --> 01:17:25,621
He took that item and he hit Abu Musa(ابوموسى) on the head.

896
01:17:27,307 --> 01:17:28,727
 And he said: Take it back to Bait-Ul-Maal(بيت المال).

897
01:17:33,529 --> 01:17:34,829
I want to make a comment here

898
01:17:35,764 --> 01:17:42,276
Abu Musa Al-Asha’ari(ابوموسى العشعري) has no blood relations with whatsoever, with the wife of Umar(عُمَر).

899
01:17:43,943 --> 01:17:50,995
They are foreign to each other, Non-Mahram(محرم) and Abu Musa(ابوموسى) is giving her a gift.

900
01:17:53,920 --> 01:17:58,604
If that were the conduct of the Sahabah(صحابه) it shows you how tight they were?

901
01:18:00,784 --> 01:18:10,584
Ya’ani(يعني) for somebody to come and give the wife of his friend a gift shows you how tight and close the relationship was.

902
01:18:11,979 --> 01:18:16,583
And how close Abu Musa(ابوموسى) was to Umar(عُمَر) and how close Sahabah(صحابه) were, they were like one family.

903
01:18:18,684 --> 01:18:21,696
Because, why would Abu Musa(ابوموسى) give the wife of Umar(عُمَر) a gift?

904
01:18:22,989 --> 01:18:27,989
But it shows that they had extremely close, and loyal, and brotherly relationship

905
01:18:28,402 --> 01:18:32,787
to the extent that Abu Musa(ابوموسى) can give the wife of Umar(عُمَر) a gift.

906
01:18:33,111 --> 01:18:38,611
 Now, Umar(عُمَر) did not agree with that because he felt that this is a preferred treatment

907
01:18:39,144 --> 01:18:43,436
just because she is the wife of Umar(عُمَر) doesn't entitle her to get gifts.

908
01:18:43,996 --> 01:18:46,896
Because as he sees it, as a conflict of interest.

909
01:18:47,694 --> 01:18:50,706
He is the Khalifah(خليفه), he shouldn't be getting gifts.

910
01:18:51,509 --> 01:18:54,621
Especially from someone who is appointed by him, as a Governor.

911
01:18:55,827 --> 01:19:04,827
Money shouldn't be used in such a way, by the way its the money of Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari(أبوموسى ألعشعري)

912
01:19:04,909 --> 01:19:07,609
and he gave it to the wife of umar(عمر) as a gift.

913
01:19:10,534 --> 01:19:13,334
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very strict with his wives,

914
01:19:13,492 --> 01:19:16,804
he didn’t want them to intervene in the affairs of state.

915
01:19:17,797 --> 01:19:21,997
Once he was writing a letter reprimanding one of his governors,

916
01:19:22,743 --> 01:19:26,443
so the wife of Umar(عُمَر) came and she said: Why are you being so harsh on him?

917
01:19:26,839 --> 01:19:32,119
He said: You stay quiet go and do your stitching and stay away from the affairs of government.

918
01:19:33,212 --> 01:19:36,808
Sometimes, the comments of Umar(عُمَر) were bit harsh and rough, and

919
01:19:37,633 --> 01:19:40,565
and I hope that sisters will still going to show up tomorrow.

920
01:19:41,202 --> 01:19:49,110
and you are not going to say that we wouldn't accept such statements.

921
01:19:49,221 --> 01:19:53,721
Ya’ni(يعني) Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he was disciplining his wives

922
01:19:53,802 --> 01:19:55,231
and that was the way of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب),

923
01:19:55,389 --> 01:19:58,541
he didn't want his women to involve in the affairs of government.

924
01:19:59,792 --> 01:20:04,692
Rasool Allah ﷺ would seek the advice of his wives.

925
01:20:06,304 --> 01:20:08,892
Like for example, with Umm Salamah(ام سلمه) in Sulah-Hudaybiya(صلح الحديبيه),

926
01:20:08,973 --> 01:20:12,125
she was the one who gave him the Nasihaa(نصيحه) of

927
01:20:14,155 --> 01:20:19,583
Rasool Allah ﷺ, going himself and shaving his head slaughtering his animals.

928
01:20:21,158 --> 01:20:26,690
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he didn’t want his women to involve in the affairs of state.

929
01:20:36,555 --> 01:20:39,639
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) received some money,

930
01:20:39,934 --> 01:20:42,090
so Hafsa(حفصه), Umm-Ul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين) came to Umar(عُمَر) and said,

931
01:20:42,169 --> 01:20:46,409
Don’t forget your relatives, you need to give to your relatives, you need to make, Sula-Tur-Rahem(صلحةالرحم)

932
01:20:46,887 --> 01:20:49,587
you need to be kind to your kinship,

933
01:20:50,226 --> 01:20:59,446
and she was telling him about your rights and duties towards your family - the clan of Bannu Udae(بنوعدي).

934
01:21:01,189 --> 01:21:03,121
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he stopped her and he said:

935
01:21:03,575 --> 01:21:08,383
غَشَشْتِيْ أَبَاكِيْ، وَ نَصَحْتِيْ أَقَارِبِكْ

936
01:21:09,398 --> 01:21:18,802
You have cheated your father by being nice and well to your family.

937
01:21:20,071 --> 01:21:22,071
He said; This money belongs to the Muslims.

938
01:21:23,415 --> 01:21:28,879
I would give my relatives from my own personal money not from the money that belongs to the Muslims.

939
01:21:29,290 --> 01:21:35,614
So, he said; you cheated your father, meaning, you are not doing your father good by giving me this Naseeha(نصيحه),

940
01:21:37,249 --> 01:21:38,985
even though you are benefiting your relatives.

941
01:21:41,568 --> 01:21:44,835
So, he was very strict with his house hold.

942
01:21:46,352 --> 01:21:50,720
Now, how would Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) treat the house hold of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Ahlul-Bait(اهل البيت).?

943
01:21:52,638 --> 01:21:56,354
 He used to take special care of Ummahatul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين),

944
01:21:57,559 --> 01:22:04,408
he used to love Al-Hassan wal-Hussain(الحسن ولحسين), Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), Al-Abbas(العباس) and his son Abdullah(عبدالله)

945
01:22:05,797 --> 01:22:09,396
and he used to put them in a very high status.

946
01:22:11,354 --> 01:22:16,454
When he would send money to the house hold of Rasool Allah ﷺ

947
01:22:17,471 --> 01:22:21,371
he would give them, so much and incase there is any shortage,

948
01:22:21,732 --> 01:22:26,030
the shortage would be in the share of his own daughter, Hafsa(حفصه)

949
01:22:28,149 --> 01:22:29,499
that’s where the shortage would be.

950
01:22:30,112 --> 01:22:34,808
In what he gives to Hafsa(حفصه) the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ why?

951
01:22:34,950 --> 01:22:36,117
Because she is his daughter.

952
01:22:37,728 --> 01:22:41,428
 Once he gave Zaynab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش), so much money,

953
01:22:41,890 --> 01:22:50,302
huge pile of coins, so when Zaynab(زينب) saw that she said;

954
01:22:50,609 --> 01:22:53,165
"May Allah forgive Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

955
01:22:54,857 --> 01:23:00,937
 There are other wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who would do a better job in distributing this money.

956
01:23:01,886 --> 01:23:05,094
" He told her, no, no , no this is not for distribution, this is yours.

957
01:23:06,160 --> 01:23:11,856
She thought that, he is bringing her the money to distribute among the rest of Ummahatul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين)

958
01:23:12,390 --> 01:23:15,382
but she was told that all of this is your portion.

959
01:23:16,568 --> 01:23:21,992
She was so terrified, by the amount of it, she told her servants to cover it with a cloth.

960
01:23:22,985 --> 01:23:24,065
It was so much for her.

961
01:23:25,487 --> 01:23:28,887
 And then she told her servants to put her hand under the cloth

962
01:23:29,867 --> 01:23:36,667
and take out from it and go and give it to orphans, to widows, to Miskeen(مسكين) to the needy

963
01:23:37,752 --> 01:23:44,692
and the pile was decreasing going down, going down going down, until her servant said:

964
01:23:45,812 --> 01:23:49,852
 "O Umm-Ul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين), Zaynab(زينب)! Why don’t you leave some for us? We have a right in it."

965
01:23:51,251 --> 01:23:54,075
So, then Zaynab(زينب) said, alright take what is under that cloth.

966
01:23:54,207 --> 01:23:57,115
They uncovered it and there were more than Eighty Dirham(درهم) left.

967
01:23:59,996 --> 01:24:06,228
Zaynab(زينب) she was so, terrified with this amount of money, the whole concept of all of this wealth coming in.

968
01:24:06,660 --> 01:24:09,536
You know, in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ they were so poor.

969
01:24:10,224 --> 01:24:15,024
A month would pass by without ever having a hot meal.

970
01:24:18,909 --> 01:24:21,409
Zaynab(زينب) raised her hands up and said: "O Allah!

971
01:24:23,633 --> 01:24:30,525
Don’t allow me to live until, the next time Umar(عُمَر) gives me At'ta(عطاء)."

972
01:24:32,156 --> 01:24:33,456
And she died soon after that.

973
01:24:35,266 --> 01:24:38,922
She felt that this wealth is a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) I don’t want to see this again.

974
01:24:39,222 --> 01:24:41,866
So O Allah! take me away before this happens.

975
01:24:43,329 --> 01:24:45,877
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ accepted her Dua(دُعَا) and she died.

976
01:24:46,059 --> 01:24:51,191
She was the first of the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ to pass away.

977
01:24:55,430 --> 01:24:58,830
The wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ Ummahatul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين)

978
01:24:59,607 --> 01:25:09,739
were urging Umar(عُمَر) to allow them to make Hajj(حَجْ) and he was refusing but when they insisted, he agreed.

979
01:25:11,056 --> 01:25:18,160
And he told Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) and Sa’ad Bin Abi Waqas(سعد بن ابي وقاص) to accompany them

980
01:25:18,608 --> 01:25:24,188
and he said; One of you be in front and one of you should be in back and don’t walk with them.

981
01:25:25,353 --> 01:25:26,496
Because they are non Mahram(محرم).

982
01:25:27,337 --> 01:25:29,456
So, he said; Don’t walk with them.

983
01:25:29,604 --> 01:25:31,371
You walk one ahead and one behind.

984
01:25:32,138 --> 01:25:39,770
 And he said; Whenever they spend the night you have them stay in a protected area and you stand and guard them.

985
01:25:40,902 --> 01:25:46,246
And in Tawaf(طواف) do not allow any man to make Tawaf(طواف) with them, Only woman can make Tawaf(طواف) with them.

986
01:25:46,676 --> 01:25:49,528
 He was giving special care to Ummahatul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين).

987
01:25:49,816 --> 01:25:52,752
Nobody would ever be prevented from Tawaf(طواف).

988
01:25:53,816 --> 01:25:58,492
The only exception was when Ummahatul-Mo’mineen(امهات المؤمنين) are making Tawaf(طواف) no men are allowed there,

989
01:25:58,895 --> 01:26:00,639
so only women can make Tawaf(طواف) with them.

990
01:26:01,914 --> 01:26:07,214
These were exceptional rules that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had for Ummahatul-Mo’mineen رضي الله عنهن.

991
01:26:09,082 --> 01:26:14,582
And as I have said; he was very close to Ali(علي), he was one of his senior advisors,

992
01:26:15,327 --> 01:26:18,011
and he used to love Al-Hassan wal Hussain(الحسن ولحسين).

993
01:26:18,630 --> 01:26:25,230
 Al-Hussain Ibn Ali(الحسين ابن علي) said and Al-Hussain(الحسين) was young, very young at that time,

994
01:26:25,852 --> 01:26:32,692
he said; Umar(عُمَر) saw me once and he told me, O my son! Why don’t you visit me?

995
01:26:34,629 --> 01:26:35,929
How come you are not visiting me?

996
01:26:37,563 --> 01:26:39,671
 So, Al-Hussain(الحسين) said; I will Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين).

997
01:26:41,635 --> 01:26:43,420
Al-Hussain(الحسين) said: I went to visit Umar(عُمَر)

998
01:26:43,500 --> 01:26:50,593
and he was having a private session with Muawiya Ibn Abi Sufiyan(معاويه ابن ابي سفيان).

999
01:26:51,405 --> 01:26:56,137
And Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) was standing at the door and he wasn’t even giving permission to come in.

1000
01:26:56,191 --> 01:26:59,799
Even Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) wasn’t allowed to enter the room

1001
01:27:00,614 --> 01:27:02,838
- because Umar(عُمَر) was meeting privately with Muawiya(معاويه).

1002
01:27:04,158 --> 01:27:09,658
Al-Hussain(الحسين) said: When I saw Abdullah Ibn Umar(عبدالله ابن عمر) himself walking away,

1003
01:27:10,567 --> 01:27:14,043
I didn’t bother asking for permission to go in, so I left.

1004
01:27:15,291 --> 01:27:21,123
A while later Umar(عُمَر) meets me and he says, O my son! How come you didn’t visit me?

1005
01:27:22,374 --> 01:27:24,031
Al-Hussain(الحسين) said: Well I did visit you

1006
01:27:24,097 --> 01:27:28,166
but you were meeting with Muawiya(معاويه) and Abdullah(عبدالله) wasn’t even given the permission to go in,

1007
01:27:28,226 --> 01:27:29,426
so I didn’t ask for permission.

1008
01:27:30,677 --> 01:27:32,505
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: O my son!

1009
01:27:33,363 --> 01:27:42,959
I would give you priority over my own son, Abdullah(عبدالله) because you are in my head.

1010
01:27:43,509 --> 01:27:49,973
Umar(عُمَر) placed his hand on the head of Al-Hussain(الحسين) and he said; It is Allah and then you.

1011
01:27:51,271 --> 01:27:53,938
For me, it is Allah and then you.

1012
01:27:54,897 --> 01:28:02,421
That was the love that he had to Al-Hussain(الحسين) and Al-Hassan(الحسن) the sons of Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

1013
01:28:10,537 --> 01:28:23,373
Al-Abbas(العباس) and Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنهم had a financial dispute Ali(علي) and his uncle Abbas(العباس).

1014
01:28:24,874 --> 01:28:29,474
So, they came in to meet with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and Umar(عُمَر) had Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف),

1015
01:28:29,869 --> 01:28:35,537
 Az-Zubair Bin Al-Awam(الزبير بن عوام), Sa’ad bin Abi Waqas(سعد بن ابي وقاص), some other Sahabah(صحابه), Uthman(عثمان).

1016
01:28:37,045 --> 01:28:41,837
So, Uthman(عثمان) said; O Ameer-Ul-Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين) why don’t you judge between these two men and get it over with.

1017
01:28:42,372 --> 01:28:44,172
The dispute has been going on for some time.

1018
01:28:45,925 --> 01:28:47,625
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said; Slow down,

1019
01:28:51,454 --> 01:29:02,867
Didn’t you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ said that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) do not leave behind any inheritance.

1020
01:29:04,656 --> 01:29:08,208
إِنَّا مَعْشَرَ الْأَنْبِيَاءِ لَا نُوْرَثْ مَا تَرَكْنَاه’ صَدَقَهْ

1021
01:29:08,547 --> 01:29:13,083
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that we the prophets do not leave behind inheritance.

1022
01:29:13,210 --> 01:29:15,574
What we leave behind is charity, is Sadaqah(صدقه).

1023
01:29:16,922 --> 01:29:20,442
So, this is an exception from the rule of inheritance.

1024
01:29:21,085 --> 01:29:25,393
Inheritance usually goes to the family members but the exception are with the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

1025
01:29:28,637 --> 01:29:35,861
They said; Yes! Umar(عُمَر) asked Ali(علي) and Abbas(عباس), he said: Don't you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ  said that?

1026
01:29:35,947 --> 01:29:36,647
They said: Yes!."

1027
01:29:38,060 --> 01:29:46,860
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: And you know that Rasool Allah ﷺ in his days, he used to live off the Fai(فيئ),

1028
01:29:47,306 --> 01:29:50,606
the spoils of war that came from Bannu Nadhir(بنو نضير).

1029
01:29:51,931 --> 01:29:59,731
What he used to do is he use to take from it, enough to support his family for a year

1030
01:29:59,756 --> 01:30:02,656
and then the rest would give it out in Sadaqah(صدقه), isn’t that true?

1031
01:30:02,753 --> 01:30:04,686
They said; Yes!, that’s true.

1032
01:30:07,410 --> 01:30:14,110
Umar(عُمَر) said; And when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) held on to that land

1033
01:30:15,486 --> 01:30:22,278
and he would give you enough for a year and he would spend the rest in Sadaqah(صدقه), isn’t that true?

1034
01:30:22,652 --> 01:30:24,185
Ali(علي) and Abbas(عباس) said; "Yes!".

1035
01:30:25,630 --> 01:30:31,430
 Umar(عُمَر) said: And then when I became Khalifah(خليفه) for the first two years of my life that's was what I was doing.

1036
01:30:31,727 --> 01:30:39,099
 I would take what Rasool Allah ﷺ used to take and would give it to you, Ali(علي) your portion goes to your wife Fatima(فاطمه)

1037
01:30:39,140 --> 01:30:41,040
 because she is daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ

1038
01:30:41,336 --> 01:30:47,152
 and Al-Abbas(العباس), because you were asking for your portion from Muhammadﷺ being his uncle

1039
01:30:47,782 --> 01:30:49,926
and I used to give you that isn’t that true?

1040
01:30:50,114 --> 01:30:51,054
 They said: Yes!.

1041
01:30:52,042 --> 01:30:58,786
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: And then I gave it to you because you asked me for it.

1042
01:30:59,490 --> 01:31:05,190
And you said, that you will follow the same way that I was following,

1043
01:31:05,323 --> 01:31:11,523
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was following and Rasool Allah ﷺ was following in distributing the harvest of this land

1044
01:31:11,950 --> 01:31:14,222
and you agreed to that and you took it from me.

1045
01:31:14,567 --> 01:31:17,987
And now you are coming and complaining that you are having a dispute among you.

1046
01:31:18,289 --> 01:31:20,289
I am not going to make any ruling among you.

1047
01:31:20,636 --> 01:31:26,076
You either follow the same way or you give it back to me and I will take care of it.

1048
01:31:28,369 --> 01:31:34,245
So, when it came to following the rules, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would follow the rules strictly,

1049
01:31:35,254 --> 01:31:43,010
and even though he had the love of the house hold of Rasool Allah ﷺ but in this particular situation,

1050
01:31:43,094 --> 01:31:46,326
he told Al-Abbas(العباس) and Ali(علي) either you are up to it,

1051
01:31:46,405 --> 01:31:49,657
and you can take care of that land yourself and not fight among you

1052
01:31:50,063 --> 01:31:54,735
or you give it back to me and I will be the one to manage it.

1053
01:31:59,139 --> 01:31:59,439
Tayeb(طيب),

1054
01:31:59,553 --> 01:32:02,853
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

1055
01:32:03,063 --> 01:32:07,063
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY

1056
01:32:07,193 --> 01:32:11,373
MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

1057
01:32:11,467 --> 01:32:15,507
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW

1058
01:32:15,778 --> 01:32:19,378
MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE

